"use strict";(globalThis.webpackChunkwebsite=globalThis.webpackChunkwebsite||[]).push([[130],{7735(e){e.exports=JSON.parse('{"archive":{"blogPosts":[{"id":"welcome-to-wledger","metadata":{"permalink":"/blog/welcome-to-wledger","editUrl":"https://github.com/tuxedocurly/wledger/tree/main/website/blog/2026-01-14-wledger-launch.md","source":"@site/blog/2026-01-14-wledger-launch.md","title":"Welcome to WLEDger","description":"The story behind WLEDger - CTRL + F for physical objects.","date":"2026-01-14T00:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":false,"label":"General","permalink":"/blog/tags/general","description":"General posts about WLEDger."}],"readingTime":1.86,"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[{"name":"Colton (TuxedoMakes)","title":"WLEDger Dev, Maker of Things","url":"https://github.com/tuxedocurly","page":{"permalink":"/blog/authors/tuxedomakes"},"socials":{"github":"https://github.com/tuxedocurly","kofi":"https://ko-fi.com/tuxedomakes","youtube":"https://www.youtube.com/@TuxedoMakes"},"imageURL":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3431855?v=4","key":"tuxedomakes"}],"frontMatter":{"slug":"welcome-to-wledger","title":"Welcome to WLEDger","authors":["tuxedomakes"],"tags":["general"]},"unlisted":false},"content":"The story behind WLEDger - CTRL + F for physical objects.\\n\\n\x3c!-- truncate --\x3e\\n\\n### The Problem\\nAs a maker and serial hobbyist, I\'ve accumulated a massive amount of \\"stuff\\" to support my cycle of making.\\n\\nOver time, this accumulation led to a major bottleneck: I couldn\'t remember what parts I had or where they were stored. This resulted in accidental over-buying and under-utilizing the parts I already owned. I wanted a system that solved these problems so I could get back to doing what I love: **making things.**\\n\\nI needed an inventory system that was self-hostable and privacy-respecting. Most tools I found were either closed source, expensive commercial software, or abandonware.\\n\\n### Inspiration\\nWLEDger stands on the shoulders of giants. Two projects specifically inspired this journey:\\n\\n1. **[Zack Freedman\'s LED Gridfinity Project](https://youtu.be/7WAhquGQq3o?si=W-1QXX9IZ2f_B7Vp):** Zack\'s approach is cool, but expensive and impractical. I store things in random containers, shelves, and boxes, so I needed a more flexible solution.\\n2. **[MIMOSA / Spotlight Storage](https://github.com/FireMarshmellow/Spotlight_Storage):** This was much closer to my needs. It utilizes WLED to help users search for *and* locate items. However, the project hasn\'t been updated in over two years.\\n\\n### Introducing WLEDger\\nGiven the state of the existing ecosystem, I decided to build the tool I wanted to use. WLEDger is a modern inventory system that features:\\n\\n* **Visual Stock Location:** Use WLED to light up the location of your parts, and view your entire inventory status at a glance.\\n* **Custom Dashboards:** Organize your inventory \\"containers\\" into custom views called \\"walls\\".\\n* **Multi-User Support:** Authentication and user management with an optional guest mode.\\n* **Rich Part Management:** Track details, quantities, urls, datasheets, and more.\\n* **Ranked Search:** Find what you need instantly.\\n* **Data Safety & Convenience:** Built-in backup, restore, and bulk import tools.\\n* ... and much more!\\n\\nWLEDger is the organizational maker tool I\'ve been searching for. It\'s become an *essential* part of my workflow.\\n\\nI hope you find WLEDger useful! My plan is to maintain and support WLEDger long into the future. If you have a feature request, feel free to submit an Issue on GitHub, or reach out to me on Discord.\\n\\nCheck out the documentation to get started, or view the source on GitHub!\\n\\nHappy Making."}]}}')}}]);